d"} {"question" "q-130155" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+3{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+3=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe auxiliary equation has pure imaginary roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+3 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-3 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-130155" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0482831521116e3467a76cdb107108638d7d5531b5dd69b53e1c1b2caa227465"} {"question" "q-130155" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-130155" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\sqrt{3