my/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-130164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+6\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+109{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +109) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +109=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +109 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +9)-9+109 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2}+100 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2} & =-100 \\\\ \\lambda +3 & =\\pm 10\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-3\\pm 10\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  $\\lambda =-3\\pm 10\\text{i}$ are the complex roots of the auxiliary equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-130164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0482831521116e3467a76cdb107108638d7d5531b5dd69b53e1c1b2caa227465"} {"question" "q-130164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.