ligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+12\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+40{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+12\\lambda +40) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+12\\lambda +40=0\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+12\\lambda +40 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+12\\lambda +36)-36+40 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +6)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +6)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ \\lambda +6 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-6\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  $\\lambda =-6\\pm 2\\text{i}$ are the complex roots of the auxiliary equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-64694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0482831521116e3467a76cdb107108638d7d5531b5dd69b53e1c1b2caa227465"} {"question" "q-64694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-64694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3\\pm 10\\text{i}"] ["math" "-6\\pm 2\\text{i}"] ["math" "6\\pm 3\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\pm 2\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\pm 6\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-64694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6\\pm 2\\text{i}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-90799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the equation ${y}^{″}+3y=0,$ where $y=y(t).$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ is a solution, then $\\lambda =$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-90799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}+3{e}^{\\lambda t} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda t}({\\lambda }^{2}+3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+3=0.\n$$\n\nSolving the auxiliary equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+3 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-3 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  $\\lambda =\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}$ are the (purely imaginary) roots of the auxiliary equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-90799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0482831521116e3467a76cdb107108638d7d5531b5dd69b53e1c1b2caa227465"} {"question" "q-90799" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-90799" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}"] ["math" "1\\pm 3\\text{i}"] ["math" "3\\pm \\text{i}"] ["math" "\\pm 3\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-90799" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-90802" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+8y=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-90802" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-4\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+8{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +8) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +8=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4)-4+8 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ \\lambda -2 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =2\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-90802" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0482831521116e3467a76cdb107108638d7d5531b5dd69b53e1c1b2caa227465"} {"question" "q-90802" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-90802" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y={e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)"] ["math" "y={e}^{-4x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)"] ["math" "y={e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)"] ["math" "y={e}^{4x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)"] ["math" "y={e}^{x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-90802" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-7818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+26y=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-7818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+26{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +26) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +26=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +26 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +1)-1+26 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2}+25 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2} & =-25 \\\\ \\lambda +1 & =\\pm 5\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-1\\pm 5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-7818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0482831521116e3467a76cdb107108638d7d5531b5dd69b53e1c1b2caa227465"} {"question" "q-7818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-7818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y={e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)"] ["math" "y={e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)"] ["math" "y={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)"] ["math" "y={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)"] ["math" "y={e}^{x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/