bda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+1) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+1=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nSolving the auxiliary equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm \\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $\\lambda =\\pm \\text{i}$ are the purely imaginary roots of the auxiliary equation. \n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions $\\text{Re}({e}^{\\text{i}x})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $\\text{Im}({e}^{\\text{i}x})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ is not a solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-130335" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0482831521116e3467a76cdb107108638d7d5531b5dd69b53e1c1b2caa227465"} {"question" "q-130335" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-130335" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-130335" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-64698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=y(t)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}+64y=0,$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-64698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}+64{e}^{\\lambda t} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda t}({\\lambda }^{2}+64) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+64=0.\n$$\n\nSolving the auxiliary equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+64 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-64 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm 8\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $\\lambda =\\pm 8\\text{i}$ are the (purely imaginary) roots of the auxiliary equation. \n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions $\\text{Re}({e}^{8\\text{i}t})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡8t$ and $\\text{Im}({e}^{8\\text{i}t})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡8t$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $\\operatorname{sin}⁡8t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t$ is not a solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-64698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0482831521116e3467a76cdb107108638d7d5531b5dd69b53e1c1b2caa227465"} {"question" "q-64698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-64698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡8t"] ["math" "-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡8t+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡8t}{4}"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡8t"] ["math" "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡8t-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡8t"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡8t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-64698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡8t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-130336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=y(x)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+17y=0,$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-130336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+8\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+17{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +17) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +17=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +17 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +16)-16+17 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\lambda +4 & =\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-4\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =-4\\pm \\text{i}$ are the complex roots of the auxiliary equation.\n\nThus, any linear combination of the functions $\\text{Re}({e}^{(-4+\\text{i})x})={e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $\\text{Im}({e}^{(-4+\\text{i})x})={e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only ${e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4{e}^{x}$ is not a solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-130336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0482831521116e3467a76cdb107108638d7d5531b5dd69b53e1c1b2caa227465"} {"question" "q-130336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-130336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "2{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "4{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "9{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4{e}^{x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-130336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4{e}^{x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-130330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=y(x)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+50y=0,$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-130330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+50{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +50) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +50=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +50 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +1)-1+50 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2}+49 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2} & =-49 \\\\ \\lambda +1 & =\\pm 7\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-1\\pm 7\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =-1\\pm 7\\text{i}$ are the complex roots of the auxiliary equation.\n\nThus, any linear combination of the functions $\\text{Re}({e}^{(-1+7\\text{i})x})={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x$ and $\\text{Im}({e}^{(-1+7\\text{i})x})={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $50{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x$ is not a solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064047/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f2c955db89ff2206ed531f593a149661417e293b1cffba8bae7ce025cdce38d"} {"question" "q-130330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_